WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:05.060
- [Narrator] An American
hero is on that train.

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:07.250
Her name?
Kate Warne.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.300
She was the first woman
detective in the U.S.,

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.970
and on that very train she
saved Abraham Lincoln's life.

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:18.137
(train whistle blows)

00:00:22.152 --> 00:00:23.910
When Kate Warne applied for a position in

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:25.570
the Pinkerton Detective Agency,

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:27.880
the detectives tried to turn her away.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.640
They didn't think a
woman could do the job.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:32.060
Kate argued the women can be

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:35.060
very good at uncovering secrets.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:36.500
She won the men over and became

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.640
America's first female detective.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.800
She proved to be a gifted investigator,

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.940
working many cases and going undercover

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:46.050
in the years leading up to the Civil War.

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:50.240
In disguise as a rich southern socialite,

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:52.180
Kate uncovered a plot to assassinate

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:54.290
newly-elected Abraham Lincoln.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.140
The killers planned to intercept him along

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:01.280
the train route on his way to take office.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.800
Kate and her agency worked
with the president-elect

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.600
to carry out a daring plan.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:09.030
After a dinner in Philadelphia,

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:10.570
Lincoln threw on a disguise and

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.610
snuck to the train depot in secret.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:16.080
He met up with Kate,
who posed as his sister.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.240
She had bribed the conductor to reserve

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:20.790
the back of the train car to hide

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:23.250
her and the undercover president-elect.

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:26.960
The plan was a success.

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:30.690
Kate stood guard over
Lincoln while he slept.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:33.120
Neither his assassins
or the other passengers

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:34.470
knew he was on the train.

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:38.400
Legend has it her watchful eye during

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.410
that sleepless night is the inspiration

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.070
for the term private eye.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:45.720
American history could
have forever been changed,

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:49.300
if not for the first female
detective, Kate Warne.

